## Total Recall — Codebase Architecture

Total Recall is a **filesystem-native AI memory system** distributed as an npm package (`total-recall`). It provides portable, persistent memory for AI coding assistants by storing knowledge as Markdown files with SSSS (Structured Semantic Syntax System) YAML frontmatter. There is no database — the filesystem is the brain.

### Core Architecture

```
total-recall/
├── src/
│   ├── cli/              # CLI commands (remember, recall, forget, compile, etc.)
│   ├── core/             # Core engine (surface compiler, embeddings, optimizer, etc.)
│   └── server/           # REST API server + route modules
├── frontend/             # React dashboard UI (Vite + TypeScript)
│   └── src/
│       ├── pages/        # Route pages (Chat, Vault, Graph, Settings, etc.)
│       ├── components/   # Shared UI components
│       └── api/          # API client modules
├── .agent/
│   ├── skills/           # Agent skills (this directory)
│   └── secrets.enc       # Encrypted secrets (AES-256-GCM)
├── docs/                 # Documentation, project trackers, guides
├── scaffold/             # Template files for new installs
└── modules/              # Nested packages (NOT agent skills)
    └── skill-deploy/     # Skill deployment module
```

### Key Subsystems

1. **CLI (`src/cli/`)**: Entry point is `src/cli/index.mjs`. Commands: `remember`, `recall`, `forget`, `compile`, `repo-expert`, `config`, `ingest`.
2. **Surface Compiler (`src/core/surface.mjs`)**: Reads all memory nodes from the vault, compiles them into instruction files (AGENTS.md, INSTRUCTIONS.md, GEMINI.md, CLAUDE.md) that get injected into IDE agents.
3. **Dream Cycle (`src/core/optimizer.mjs`, `clarity-rewriter.mjs`, `fact-seeker.mjs`)**: Background optimization pipeline that evaluates memory staleness, discovers knowledge gaps, and rewrites unclear nodes. Calls external LLM APIs — no local models.
4. **REST Server (`src/server/`)**: Express server with route modules under `src/server/routes/`. Serves the dashboard UI and provides API endpoints for memory operations.
5. **Frontend Dashboard (`frontend/`)**: React + Vite app. Pages: Chat, Vault, Graph, Tasks, Integrations, Skills, Keys, Settings, Help, Onboarding.
6. **Embeddings (`src/core/embeddings.mjs`)**: Generates vector embeddings for semantic search. Uses external embedding API.

### Memory Architecture

Memory nodes live in `.agent/skills/total-recall/memory-vault/` as individual `.md` files with SSSS frontmatter. Categories: `invariant`, `correction`, `preference`, `concept`, `pattern`, `decision`, `fact`, `log`.

Derived indexes live in `.agent/skills/total-recall/memory-derived/`:
- `graph-index.jsonl` — node relationships
- `memory-layers.jsonl` — layered memory tiers
- `skill-routes.jsonl` — skill routing index
- `embeddings.db` — vector store

### No Local Models

Total Recall does NOT run local AI models. All LLM calls go to external APIs (configured via API keys). The system prompts in `src/core/` files are sent to these external APIs for the Dream Cycle optimization pipeline.

